    "text": {
     "en": "After Harsha's empire broke up, three powers, the Palas of Bengal, the Pratiharas of the west and the Rashtrakutas of the Deccan, fought for control of Kannauj, a rich city on the Ganga.\nThe Palas ruled Bengal and Bihar and supported Buddhist centres like Nalanda and Vikramashila. The Rashtrakutas built the rock-cut Kailasa temple at Ellora.\nThe long struggle weakened all three."
    }
